3. Target Audience
3.1 General Workshop Audience
The product shall remain discoverable and usable as an interesting Garry’s Mod Workshop map.
A player may initially encounter it while searching for:
•	scripted maps;
•	reactor maps;
•	science-fiction maps;
•	interactive maps;
•	sandbox maps;
•	power-plant simulations;
•	cinematic experiences.
3.2 Core Audience
The primary long-term audience is expected to include players who:
•	enjoy complex reactor-operation games;
•	enjoy technical or industrial simulations;
•	are willing to read documentation;
•	are comfortable experimenting with complicated systems;
•	are experienced with Garry’s Mod;
•	enjoy operating large fictional machinery;
•	appreciate advanced Source or Lua map scripting.
3.3 Accessibility Expectation
The map does not need to be immediately understandable to every Workshop user.
However:
•	important controls shall be labeled;
•	current system states shall be observable;
•	blocking conditions should be communicated;
•	dangerous actions should provide warnings;
•	the cause of major failures should be discoverable;
•	external documentation should be sufficient to operate the reactor correctly.
