6. Publication and Showable State
6.1 Definition of Showable
The project shall be considered showable when the Dark Fusion Reactor map can be publicly demonstrated alongside a publishable version of the Luasquare framework.
“Showable” does not necessarily mean that every planned mechanic is implemented.
At minimum, a showable build should demonstrate:
•	a working separately installed Luasquare addon;
•	a Dark Fusion Reactor map that requires Luasquare;
•	successful map bootstrap;
•	Lua-owned simulation state;
•	working Hammer entity integration;
•	functional reactor controls;
•	working 3D2D instrumentation;
•	at least one complete reactor operating path;
•	framework debugging sufficient to diagnose major problems;
•	enough stability for a public technical demonstration.
6.2 Final Public Release
The final public release is expected to require more than the initial showable build.
Final-release requirements may include:
•	complete startup paths;
•	dark-fusion operation;
•	shutdown procedures;
•	fuel production;
•	major disasters;
•	DECAOS subtitles;
•	dynamic music;
•	operator scoring;
•	multiplayer validation;
•	documentation;
•	Workshop dependency configuration.
