9. Luasquare Design Goal
9.1 Mapper-Friendly Operation
Luasquare shall be designed for map creators who want to build complex scripted systems without implementing the entire system through Source I/O.
The framework should allow a mapper to:
1.	place Source entities in Hammer;
2.	assign targetnames;
3.	create a Lua bootstrap;
4.	register framework modules;
5.	bind modules to targetnamed entities;
6.	define simulation values and getter functions;
7.	operate the map with fewer logic entities.
9.2 Hammer Integration Philosophy
Luasquare shall not require a custom Hammer editor extension.
The framework shall use normal Hammer entities where practical.
A mapper should remain able to use:
•	info_target;
•	prop_dynamic;
•	func_button;
•	func_rot_button;
•	func_movelinear;
•	func_tracktrain;
•	logic_relay;
•	sprites;
•	lights;
•	sound entities;
•	other standard Source entities.
9.3 Source I/O Reduction
One of the framework’s principal purposes is to reduce the need for large Source I/O logic circuits.
This shall help avoid:
•	excessive logic entities;
•	difficult-to-maintain relay chains;
•	duplicated timers;
•	entity-limit pressure;
•	opaque state-machine construction;
•	manually repeated I/O connections;
•	complex debugging inside Hammer.
Source I/O shall remain valid for simple local presentation actions.
Luasquare does not need to replace every relay or every entity output.
