10.2 Current Example Bootstrap
The current RBMK experiment map uses a large map-specific bootstrap.
The bootstrap includes required packages and registers the systems used by the map.
Example:
include('luasquare_module/seg7display.lua')
include('luasquare_module/3d2display.lua')
include('luasquare_module/annunciator/annunciator.lua')
include('luasquare_module/gaugedisplay.lua')
include('luasquare_module/keypad_controller.lua')
include('luasquare_module/rod_selector.lua')
include('luasquare_powerplant/init.lua')
include('luasquare_rbmk/init.lua')
The bootstrap also registers map-specific instances.
Example:
LUASQUARE_SEG7.RegisterDisplay('reactor_mwth', {
    'reactor_mwth_0',
    'reactor_mwth_1',
    'reactor_mwth_2',
    'reactor_mwth_3',
    'reactor_mwth_4'
})

LUASQUARE_SEG7.BindDisplay('reactor_mwth', function()
    return math.floor(RBMK.LastThermalMW + RBMK.LastFlashBoilMW)
end)
The string values in this registration correspond to targetnamed Hammer entities.
10.3 Current Limitations
The current framework does not yet provide:
•	formal base classes;
•	formal module lifecycle management;
•	typed ports;
•	a visual connection graph;
•	declarative module wiring;
•	a custom editor;
•	unified reset behavior;
•	deterministic scheduling;
•	a timeline engine;
•	formal state-machine support;
•	generic Source output listeners;
•	generic control abstraction;
•	full map entity validation;
•	module-wide error containment;
•	automated bootstrap generation.
These limitations shall be accounted for when defining DFR implementation requirements.
