12. Bootstrap Requirements
12.1 Initial Implementation Direction
The first DFR bootstrap may follow the current Luasquare registration style.
Immediate development shall prioritize a functioning reactor over general bootstrap simplification.
A declarative bootstrap system or automatic registration utility may be developed later, but is not a prerequisite for the initial DFR vertical slice.
12.2 Maintainability
Although the first DFR bootstrap may be manually written, it should be divided into understandable code sections.
Suggested sections include:
•	framework includes;
•	DFR includes;
•	configuration;
•	entity bindings;
•	control registration;
•	display registration;
•	alarm registration;
•	sound and music bindings;
•	simulation startup;
•	validation;
•	debug initialization.
The bootstrap should avoid embedding large simulation functions directly inside registration blocks.
12.3 Idempotency
The current framework prevents repeated bootstrap initialization through a global initialization flag.
The DFR bootstrap shall similarly prevent accidental duplicate registration.
Until unified lifecycle support exists, a full map reload may be required after bootstrap failure or code reload.
