14. Map Entity Validation
14.1 Initialization Validation
The DFR bootstrap shall validate map bindings before beginning the reactor simulation.
Validation shall detect:
•	missing targetnames;
•	duplicate entities where one entity is expected;
•	incorrect entity classes where detectable;
•	missing critical controls;
•	missing display anchors;
•	missing relays;
•	unavailable DFR modules.
14.2 Validation Behavior
If a critical binding is missing:
•	initialization shall stop;
•	the reactor simulation shall not begin;
•	a loud Lua error or prominent console error shall be produced;
•	the missing logical binding and expected targetname shall be identified.
If a required-gameplay binding is missing:
•	initialization should stop unless a defined degraded mode exists.
If a presentation binding is missing:
•	initialization may continue;
•	a warning shall be printed;
•	the affected feature shall be marked unavailable.
If an optional binding is missing:
•	initialization may continue;
•	a lower-priority warning may be printed.
14.3 Validation Report
A future validation report should list:
•	logical binding name;
•	targetname;
•	expected entity class;
•	entities found;
•	requirement classification;
•	validation result.
A graphical validation UI is not required for the first implementation.
