15. Lua and Hammer Authority
15.1 Simulation Authority
Lua shall be authoritative for:
•	reactor state;
•	subsystem state;
•	control availability;
•	control logical position;
•	alarms;
•	damage;
•	power values;
•	fuel values;
•	startup and shutdown progression;
•	ending conditions.
Hammer entities shall represent and present the authoritative Lua state.
15.2 Control Flow
The preferred control interaction is:
Player activates Hammer control
    → Hammer invokes Luasquare or DFR
    → Server validates interaction
    → Lua updates logical state
    → Lua commands physical control movement
    → Lua commands associated relays, sounds, or effects
A control should not visually complete an invalid action before Lua validation where this can reasonably be prevented.
15.3 Source Outputs
Hammer controls may initially call Lua through existing methods such as lua_run.
A reusable Source output listener or control-discovery system may be added later.
The first implementation does not require automatic discovery of every map control.
15.4 Lua-Controlled Source Inputs
Luasquare shall use Source entity inputs where appropriate.
Examples include:
•	enabling or disabling controls;
•	locking or unlocking buttons;
•	setting button states;
•	moving func_movelinear;
•	controlling func_tracktrain;
•	activating func_rotating;
•	triggering relays;
•	setting prop skins;
•	showing or hiding sprites;
•	playing or stopping sounds.
Support for sending inputs to func_button or related controls should be added where needed so that the physical control state remains synchronized with Lua state.
