26. Initial Architectural Requirements
ARCH-001
Dark Fusion Reactor shall require the separately installed Luasquare addon.
ARCH-002
DFR-specific Lua modules shall be distributed as part of Luasquare.
ARCH-003
The DFR map addon shall contain the VMF-derived map and map-specific content.
ARCH-004
The server shall own authoritative reactor state.
ARCH-005
Hammer shall provide physical entities and targetnames.
ARCH-006
Lua shall provide simulation, control validation, alarms, displays, and state progression.
ARCH-007
The map bootstrap shall register and connect required modules manually during the initial implementation.
ARCH-008
The first implementation shall not require a visual scripting editor or Hammer extension.
ARCH-009
The framework shall support a central DFR simulation tick.
ARCH-010
The DFR simulation may slow down during server lag rather than attempting unsafe catch-up.
ARCH-011
Critical map bindings shall be validated before simulation startup.
ARCH-012
Critical Lua failures shall halt the DFR simulation.
ARCH-013
The first valid use of a temporarily contested control shall take priority.
ARCH-014
The reactor shall remain fully operable by one player.
ARCH-015
The design should allow multiple players to divide operating tasks.
ARCH-016
The normal method of starting a new session after an ending shall be reloading the map.
ARCH-017
The reactor map shall remain loaded after an ending so players may inspect the resulting environment.
ARCH-018
Simulation correctness shall take priority over exact music synchronization.
ARCH-019
The first development milestone shall be a manual annihilation-stage vertical slice.
ARCH-020
General bootstrap simplification shall not block initial DFR implementation.
